      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In the 1870s, landscape architect Frederick Law Olmsted and clergyman Thomas Starr King lobbied Senator John Conness to protect Yosemite, leading to its first national park status.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
